    "flow_gAVTzH": {
      "type": "flow",
      "blocks": {
        "media_NayzzC": {
          "type": "media",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/pexels-mikhail-nilov-8297652.jpg",
            "show_sound_control": false,
            "video_url": "",
            "video_alt_text": "",
            "enable_video_autoplay": false,
            "subheading": "",
            "heading": "OMICm Age Report",
            "image_style_heading": "square",
            "image_ratio_heading": "aspect-16/9",
            "description": "<p>This report measures your biological age using epigenetic markers across around one million DNA sites. By comparing your OMICm Age to your chronological age, the report highlights whether you are aging faster or slower than average, which has direct implications for risks of conditions like heart disease, cancer, stroke, type 2 diabetes, COPD and depression.</p>",
            "button_text": "",
            "button_link": "",
            "open_new_window_button": false,
            "show_button_style": "text-link"
          }
        },
        "media_4VUdUM": {
          "type": "media",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/pexels-mikhail-nilov-8297652.jpg",
            "show_sound_control": false,
            "video_url": "",
            "video_alt_text": "",
            "enable_video_autoplay": false,
            "subheading": "",
            "heading": "DunedinPACE Report",
            "image_style_heading": "square",
            "image_ratio_heading": "aspect-16/9",
            "description": "<p>The DunedinPACE report calculates the current pace of your biological aging. Unlike a static biological age, this \"speedometer\" tells you how quickly your body is aging right now, helping you understand whether your present lifestyle is accelerating or decelerating your aging rate.</p>",
            "button_text": "",
            "button_link": "",
            "open_new_window_button": false,
            "show_button_style": "text-link"
          }
        },
        "media_PdnWEq": {
          "type": "media",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/pexels-mikhail-nilov-8297652.jpg",
            "show_sound_control": false,
            "video_url": "",
            "video_alt_text": "",
            "enable_video_autoplay": false,
            "subheading": "",
            "heading": "Immune Report",
            "image_style_heading": "square",
            "image_ratio_heading": "aspect-16/9",
            "description": "<p>This section provides a functional assessment of your immune system through epigenetic analysis. It predicts the concentration of various immune cell types (like T-cells) and flags patterns associated with aging, disease, or immune dysregulation, providing early warnings for risks like infections or autoimmune conditions.</p>",
            "button_text": "",
            "button_link": "",
            "open_new_window_button": false,
            "show_button_style": "text-link"
          }
        },
        "media_mHeMkm": {
          "type": "media",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/pexels-mikhail-nilov-8297652.jpg",
            "show_sound_control": false,
            "video_url": "",
            "video_alt_text": "",
            "enable_video_autoplay": false,
            "subheading": "",
            "heading": "Telomere Length Report",
            "image_style_heading": "square",
            "image_ratio_heading": "aspect-16/9",
            "description": "<p>Telomeres are protective DNA caps at the end of chromosomes that shorten with cell division and age. The report estimates your telomere length, which is linked to cellular aging—shorter telomeres can indicate higher risk for age-related diseases.</p>",
            "button_text": "",
            "button_link": "",
            "open_new_window_button": false,
            "show_button_style": "text-link"
          }
        },
        "media_GKndj4": {
          "type": "media",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/pexels-mikhail-nilov-8297652.jpg",
            "show_sound_control": false,
            "video_url": "",
            "video_alt_text": "",
            "enable_video_autoplay": false,
            "subheading": "",
            "heading": "Type 2 Diabetes Risk Report",
            "image_style_heading": "square",
            "image_ratio_heading": "aspect-16/9",
            "description": "<p>This section evaluates epigenetic markers at specific gene sites (like ABCG1 and PHOSPHO1) known to be associated with increased or decreased risk for type 2 diabetes. The result provides a personalized risk score for developing type 2 diabetes based on your DNA methylation profile.</p>",
            "button_text": "",
            "button_link": "",
            "open_new_window_button": false,
            "show_button_style": "text-link"
          }
        },
        "media_Q3KKHf": {
          "type": "media",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/pexels-mikhail-nilov-8297652.jpg",
            "show_sound_control": false,
            "video_url": "",
            "video_alt_text": "",
            "enable_video_autoplay": false,
            "subheading": "",
            "heading": "Inflammation Report",
            "image_style_heading": "square",
            "image_ratio_heading": "aspect-16/9",
            "description": "<p>The inflammation report assesses DNA methylation signatures associated with inflammatory processes. Chronic inflammation can accelerate biological aging and predispose to various diseases; this section quantifies your systemic inflammation risk.</p>",
            "button_text": "",
            "button_link": "",
            "open_new_window_button": false,
            "show_button_style": "text-link"
          }
        },
        "media_Y4zz4H": {
          "type": "media",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/pexels-mikhail-nilov-8297652.jpg",
            "show_sound_control": false,
            "video_url": "",
            "video_alt_text": "",
            "enable_video_autoplay": false,
            "subheading": "",
            "heading": "Mitotic Clock Report",
            "image_style_heading": "square",
            "image_ratio_heading": "aspect-16/9",
            "description": "<p>This report estimates the rate of stem cell division in your body—a higher mitotic rate is associated with greater cancer risk and cell turnover. The mitotic clock uses methylation patterns to provide insights into your cellular replication history and risk for diseases related to excessive cell division.</p>",
            "button_text": "",
            "button_link": "",
            "open_new_window_button": false,
            "show_button_style": "text-link"
          }
        },
        "media_gn7MMt": {
          "type": "media",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/pexels-mikhail-nilov-8297652.jpg",
            "show_sound_control": false,
            "video_url": "",
            "video_alt_text": "",
            "enable_video_autoplay": false,
            "subheading": "",
            "heading": "Fitness Age Report",
            "image_style_heading": "square",
            "image_ratio_heading": "aspect-16/9",
            "description": "<p>Fitness age incorporates metrics from physical performance (like grip strength, gait speed, VO2 max) into epigenetic age calculations. The report tells you how old your body appears based on your physical fitness, highlighting the effects of exercise and lifestyle on your aging trajectory.</p>",
            "button_text": "",
            "button_link": "",
            "open_new_window_button": false,
            "show_button_style": "text-link"
          }
        },
        "media_K6N4ew": {
          "type": "media",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/pexels-mikhail-nilov-8297652.jpg",
            "show_sound_control": false,
            "video_url": "",
            "video_alt_text": "",
            "enable_video_autoplay": false,
            "subheading": "",
            "heading": "Smoking & Drinking Report",
            "image_style_heading": "square",
            "image_ratio_heading": "aspect-16/9",
            "description": "<p>This section reveals the impact of tobacco and alcohol on your epigenome. It detects methylation changes associated with these behaviors, quantifying their effect on your biological age and related disease risks.</p>",
            "button_text": "",
            "button_link": "",
            "open_new_window_button": false,
            "show_button_style": "text-link"
          }
        },
        "media_hFNwaG": {
          "type": "media",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/pexels-mikhail-nilov-8297652.jpg",
            "show_sound_control": false,
            "video_url": "",
            "video_alt_text": "",
            "enable_video_autoplay": false,
            "subheading": "",
            "heading": "Weight Loss Response Report",
            "image_style_heading": "square",
            "image_ratio_heading": "aspect-16/9",
            "description": "<p>By analyzing specific epigenetic patterns, this report predicts how effectively your body is likely to respond to weight loss interventions, helping guide personalized weight management strategies.</p>",
            "button_text": "",
            "button_link": "",
            "open_new_window_button": false,
            "show_button_style": "text-link"
          }
        },
        "media_PnNPpq": {
